  "stream": "Each `stream` is the publisher's own direct HTTPS audio, played in the page by a plain <audio> element like the World Cup player (ListenLive WC_STREAM); nothing is relayed through LP. Taken from the same station's iHeart API streams or TuneIn Tune.ashx list, MP3 preferred, session parameters dropped, and kept only when ffprobe read an audio stream from it (2026-10-07). `href` stays as the publisher page it came from.",
  "mls": "Seven direct MLS station streams verified with ffprobe on 2026-10-13; marked-verified feeds that timed out or resolved only as HLS playlists are omitted from this plain audio player.",
  "ncaaf": "Varsity Network game-audio event feeds keyed by ESPN scoreboard team code. 72 FBS team entries have direct URLs verified by ffprobe and a three-second ffmpeg decode on 2026-10-13: 52 feeds scheduled Oct 16-18, 15 additional later-dated or unlinked game feeds, two further Missouri/Purdue feeds, and three retained Iowa/Iowa State/Utah State feeds from the Oct 10 snapshot. Five discovered event URLs failed and are omitted: Charlotte, Texas State, South Alabama, Liberty and North Texas. An older Purdue URL also returned 502; Purdue’s later IM8901 feed passed. Varsity direct feeds are event-driven and can change between games, so this inventory needs refresh against the published schedule."
